{
  "project_name": "codemonkey",
  "programming_languages": [
    "Python"
  ],
  "summary": "codemonkey is a scriptable, headless coding-agent CLI (Python 3.11, uv, Typer/Rich/httpx, no LLM SDKs) that runs unattended against OpenAI-style and Anthropic-style endpoints \u2014 designed primarily for a local llama.cpp server but compatible with any OpenAI-compatible API. It provides one-shot `exec` runs with JSONL event streams and structured output via JSON schemas, an interactive REPL, session resume, diff review, execution-journal forensics, checkpoint/undo, and a golden-task eval harness, backed by 13 coding tools (shell, file read/write/edit, search, glob, repo_map, web_fetch, delegate) governed by rule-based permissions and approval policies, with pluggable compaction/memory/session strategies, prompt-cache stability, retry/backoff, and token/cost telemetry."
}
